{"repositoryId":1420675039,"availability":"available","full":"oldjazjef/hello-eme-play","name":"hello-eme-play","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-15T12:17:33Z","updated":"2026-10-17T17:45:47Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://oldjazjef.github.io/hello-eme-play/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:54:20.072Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T18:54:20.072Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T18:54:20.072Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T18:54:20.072Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Turns any website into a game, configured by one JSON. The page itself is the playing field.","The idea behind it is page navigation: the default mode has no enemies. The visitor walks or jumps over the page, knocks on elements, hops onto links and buttons to click them and takes a car for a ride. Everything else (monsters, bombs, catching, arcade games) is switched on by the configuration: a game is a navigation mode with rules on top. It works with plain HTML, any framework and any CMS. An editor (one script, no framework) and a Payload plugin change the JSON; try it in the live demo: guide, editor and live preview."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/oldjazjef/hello-eme-play/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c7724ef01475a89006170cc541803195172afbf2ccc9880e5ccaba64ab116033","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T18:54:20.164Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T18:54:20.164Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Turns any website into a game, configured by one JSON. The page itself is the playing field.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/oldjazjef/hello-eme-play/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"c7724ef01475a89006170cc541803195172afbf2ccc9880e5ccaba64ab116033","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/oldjazjef/hello-eme-play/blob